cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Coq-BBB4: a machine-checked formalization of Beeping Busy Beaver BBB(4)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Carrino"
    given-names: "John"
repository-code: "https://github.com/carrino/Coq-BBB4"
license: ISC
abstract: >-
  Kernel-checked Coq proofs (Coq 8.18, axiom footprint
  functional_extensionality_dep only) that every 4-state 2-symbol Turing
  machine either quasihalts with score at most the champion's 32,779,478
  or never quasihalts, modulo an explicitly listed and shrinking residue
  of undecided machines.  Built from the certificates of the BBB harness
  on the patterns of Coq-BB5 and busycoq.
keywords:
  - busy beaver
  - beeping busy beaver
  - quasihalting
  - Turing machines
  - Coq
  - formal verification
